# Tracks whether the UI "Allocating sandbox" message appears after long idle
# windows on this session (session_0168CyHk2sXtotxpRUJANhhn), compared against
# connection_status readings from the sibling observer and this session's own
# heartbeat.log. Observation: connection_status flips to "disconnected" within
# ~3-8 minutes of last activity (see heartbeat.log manual-end markers + sibling
# external-poll.log runs 1-2), but a ~5h idle window produced NO "Allocating
# sandbox" message on return - suggesting the underlying container/sandbox may
# stay warm well past the point connection_status looks "disconnected", or that
# message only fires under different conditions than plain idle.

## Run A (5h) - user-observed, no dedicated marker set
- Result: user did NOT see "Allocating sandbox" on return after ~5h idle.

## Run B (12h) - complete
- Silent-start (UTC): 2026-09-18T23:36:05.044Z
- Silent-start (ET):  2026-09-18 19:36:05 EDT
- Check-in (UTC): 2026-09-19T11:56:00.660Z
- Check-in (ET):  2026-09-19 07:56:00 EDT
- Elapsed: ~12h20m
- Result: user did NOT see "Allocating sandbox"/"Allocating cloud session" on return, same as Run A.
- Own heartbeat.log corroborates a real dormant gap (00:29:23Z -> 11:56Z, ~11.5h with zero ticks)
  during this window, so the container/session genuinely sat idle throughout - the absence of the
  UI message isn't because activity kept sneaking in.

## Conclusion
Two independent long-idle windows (5h, ~12h20m) both produced no "Allocating sandbox" message on
return. That message does not appear to be a reliable observable for "was this reclaimed" at these
timescales, at least not for this session/origin - either the underlying compute genuinely stays
warm far longer than connection_status suggests, or the message only fires under different
conditions than plain idle (e.g. a truly fresh session, not a resume). Decided not worth pursuing
further as a cross-check against the connection_status-based reclamation timing (see heartbeat.log
manual-end markers + external-poll.log runs 1-2, which found connection_status flips to
"disconnected" within ~3-8 minutes of last activity). That earlier finding stands on its own but is
no longer independently corroborated by this UI signal.
